MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_001: Sha Lan, let's play! I wanna play with dolls!
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_002: Alright, alright, we can play for a little bit. I'll go get\nthe one I made the other day.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_003: Sorry to bother you, Sha Lan, but can we pick up\nwhere we left off on the supply distribution?
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_004: We need to settle on a strict system if we want to\nensure everyone gets enough food.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_005: You're right. Our evacuation numbers have risen, so\nwe need to act as soon as possible.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_006: Ah!
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_007: I think I scared her off.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_008: I'm sure that's not why...
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_009: It's to be expected. I did let my hunger for vengeance\nclaim countless lives.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_010: I understand hating Dagda the Great. I was born in\nKunlun, so I empathize.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_011: You don't need to try to console me. I spent nine\nhundred years consumed with hatred for that man.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_012: I let it get more important than caring for my family.\nIt's no surprise that I'm disliked.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_013: Only after I sided with the Promised One was I able\nto remember my child's face.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_014: Mm...
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_015: I believe you know about the Dagsion prisoners of\nold. My child was taken to the imperial capital.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_016: But then Yu Phas intervened. She led two thousand\nchildren to sanctuary in Damascar.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_017: I still want to believe that my child was among\nthem. That his life was saved too.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_018: Even though I've forfeited any right I had to pray for\nmy child's well-being.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_019: That's not true, Hong Hua.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_020: I may not have children, but I know that a mother\ndoesn't need permission to pray for her child.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_021: You've been out there protecting people everywhere.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_022: Even after all these years with the terrors of the\nunderworld and the undead crawling around...
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_023: None of that begins to make up for what I did.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_024: That child—she didn't run away because she was\nscared of you.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_025: What do you mean?
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_026: Um! This is for you!
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_027: A hair clip? It's sparkling in the light...are these\nprecious stones?
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_028: Aren't they pretty? We found them buried in\nthe rubble.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_029: She wanted to make you something beautiful, despite\nthe times we're living in.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_030: This took a lot of work. Why give it to me?
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_031: You took care of my village. I wanted to make you\nsomething pretty!
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_032: We made it together, she and I. I hope you like it.\nThe children here—they really love you, Hong Hua.
MID_SE_Sar_Kou_C_033: I...thank you. I'll keep it always.